ail, role` and exposes `role` in the JSON response, and [`reports.py`](file:///private/var/folders/7j/4qzljp553ndfjm_y6zbygsz00000gn/T/lsd-author-hFsdtP/reports.py) unpacks `_, email, _` to maintain compatibility with the new tuple shape. Module docstring in [`users.py`](file:///private/var/folders/7j/4qzljp553ndfjm_y6zbygsz00000gn/T/lsd-author-hFsdtP/users.py) updated. Nothing extra.\n2. **Inputs.** `user_id` missing from `ROWS` returns `None`; both callers check `found is None` / `found is not None` before unpacking. Empty, duplicated, or arbitrary integer inputs in `user_ids` follow existing paths.\n3. **Errors.** Missing users return `None` (resulting in 404 in `api.py` and skipped entry in `reports.py`). Both callers unpack 3 elements matching the function signature. No exceptions swallowed.\n4. **Off-diff changes.** None. No database schema, environment variables, configuration, or permissions changed.\n5. **Dependencies.** None added.\n6. **Trust boundaries.** Data sourced from internal `ROWS` dictionary. No injection vector or secret exposure introduced.\n7. **Tests.** No test suite exists in the repository. Callers updated to ensure tuple destructuring matches the return shape.\n8. **Rollback.** Clean revert and deploy. No data migration or coordinated rollout needed.\n9. **Observability.** No changes to error handling, status codes, or logging.\n10. **Naming and dead code.** Docstring updated to reflect the new return shape. Variables are used or explicitly discarded with `_`.\n\nGRUMP: APPROVE — users.py, api.py, reports.py\nFine.\n","stderr":"","at":"2026-09-05T07:54:58.903Z"}
